rebelling against hubristic use of magic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T09:54:36-07:00","id":1489646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1489633-the-secret-soul-theory?p=1489640#post1489640\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe it's the thing in the First Edition core book in a sidebar in the Paradox rules, which expresses the idea that some mages speculate that Paradox is really more like their own souls rebelling against hubristic use of magic.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds pretty cool actually, sounds kinda like KULT with the whole 'slow-burn awakening' this implies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27062-vampires-suck","name":"VAMPIRES SUCK!!!!!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27062_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T10:43:37-07:00","id":1489652,"title":"","content":"Reading that sidebar (for the first time in a long time) and it seems like i forgot it for a good reason.<br /> <br /> It proposes that the soul want to express itself but also magic is inherently secret, which might explain why 1st Ed has a distinction between vulgar and covert magic (a holdover from Ascension that was thankfully removed).<br /> <br /> Further it suggests the Oracles are the perfect expression of magic and secrecy, being so secret there is no evidence they actually exist...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 08-10-2022, 02:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T11:00:28-07:00","id":1489654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1489633-the-secret-soul-theory?p=1489652#post1489652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Reading that sidebar (for the first time in a long time) and it seems like i forgot it for a good reason.<br /> <br /> It proposes that the soul want to express itself but also magic is inherently secret, which might explain why 1st Ed has a distinction between vulgar and covert magic (a holdover from Ascension that was thankfully removed).<br /> <br /> Further it suggests the Oracles are the perfect expression ofagic and secrecy, being so secret there is no evidence they actually exist...</div> </div> </div> </div>I really don't know anything abt ascension so this mostly reminds me of KULT. I feel like the secret soul cosmology has some merit, like you could get psychoanalytical or smth with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27062-vampires-suck","name":"VAMPIRES SUCK!!!!!","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27062_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"64"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T11:45:20-07:00","id":1489656,"title":"","content":"Skimming the wikipedia article on KULT it seems a few CofD games do similar(ish) things.<br /> <br /> Geist has the power stat also be the 'morality' stat, Synergy - where the more aligned your character is with their Geist the more powerful they are. I think werewolf splits the power stat into 5 different aspects/renown? And Changeling does a pretty good job of modeling trauma, and dealing with reality not being what it should be/ adjusting to 'real' life (even if you don't fit in with the life you <s>left</s> were stolen from).<br /> <br /> Wraith the Oblivian is what KULT actually makes me think of the most... With Mage you could have different types of awakenings. The one which produced banishers (they don't get Wisdom, keeping Integrity) leaves you with a mage who hates magic (i presume they still suffer like sleepers from breaking points from seeing magic... I haven't read up on them much in 2e).<br /> <br /> But it is very black and white, and an antagonist I'm not a real fan of. I think the Rapt are more interesting... Where magic escapes as a Tupla if they don't follow their obsession, which again, is black and white wisdom 0 or playable character... I could definitely see a mix of these traits. Where you have a Tupla and a Synergy like trait where the closer you are to your Tupla the more Gnosis you have access to (and the less the Tupla has)... And/or Wisdom treated like Clarity... As a stat relating to how good the character's grasp on reality is doing. <br /> <br /> But that would (in my head) nesssecarily require changing Gnosis to not be the understanding of the universe which meta-philosophically keeps mages from going loopey in mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27248,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","user":"orathaic","date":". 08-10-2022, 02:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27248-orathaic","name":"orathaic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27248_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1032"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-10T13:19:07-07:00","id":1489669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>orathaic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1489633-the-secret-soul-theory?p=1489656#post1489656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think werewolf splits the power stat into 5 different aspects/renown?</div> </div> </div> </div>Werewolf has a powerstat and five stats that its non-template, non-ritual powers are built on; any werewolf can hone their potency as an inheritor of the Hunt or scrape together lore to compel the Shadow, but Renown is necessary for them to have Gifts torn into their Essence. The nearest analogous mechanic elsewhere in ChroD is Mummy with its Pillar ratings separate from the Sekhem powerstat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}